    {
      "id": "p-bf16-weight",
      "difficulty": 4,
      "skills": [
        "gpt-hardware"
      ],
      "prose": "A weight of 6.0 is kept in bf16, which has 8 significant bits, and is updated in bf16 with no master copy.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "question": "What is the gap between bf16 numbers from 4 to 8? Give the decimal.",
          "widget": {
            "kind": "numeric",
            "answer": 0.03125,
            "tol": {
              "abs": 1e-09
            },
            "wrong": [
              {
                "id": "eps",
                "value": 0.0078125,
                "tol": {
                  "abs": 1e-09
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "half",
                "value": 0.015625,
                "tol": {
                  "abs": 1e-09
                }
              }
            ],
            "label": "Gap"
          },
          "feedback": {
            "correct": "$2^{2} \\times 2^{-7} = 2^{-5} = 0.03125$.",
            "generic": "Not quite. Scale bf16's epsilon by the power of two.",
            "byKey": {
              "eps": "That is the gap above 1; from 4 to 8 it is 4 times larger.",
              "half": "That is half the gap."
            }
          },
          "explain": {
            "text": "From $2^2$ to $2^3$ the gap is $2^{2-7} = 0.03125$."
          }
        },
        {
          "question": "With that gap of 0.03125, an update of $+0.02$ is applied. What is the stored weight? Give the decimal.",
          "widget": {
            "kind": "numeric",
            "answer": 6.03125,
            "tol": {
              "abs": 1e-09
            },
            "wrong": [
              {
                "id": "lost",
                "value": 6,
                "tol": {
                  "abs": 1e-09
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "exact",
                "value": 6.02,
                "tol": {
                  "abs": 1e-09
                }
              }
            ],
            "label": "Weight"
          },
          "feedback": {
            "correct": "6.02 is nearer 6.03125 than 6, so it rounds up.",
            "generic": "Not quite. Find the nearer bf16 neighbour of 6.02.",
            "byKey": {
              "lost": "0.02 is more than half the gap, 0.015625, so it is not lost.",
              "exact": "bf16 cannot hold 6.02."
            }
          },
          "explain": {
            "text": "$6.02$ lies 0.01125 from 6.03125 and 0.02 from 6: it becomes 6.03125."
          }
        },
        {
          "question": "The weight moved by 0.03125 instead of 0.02. By what percentage is the applied update too large? Give a percentage to 2 decimal places.",
          "widget": {
            "kind": "numeric",
            "answer": 0.5625,
            "tol": {
              "abs": 5e-05
            },
            "wrong": [
              {
                "id": "ratio",
                "value": 1.5625,
                "tol": {
                  "abs": 5e-05
                }
              }
            ],
            "label": "Too large by",
            "unit": "%",
            "over100": true
          },
          "feedback": {
            "correct": "$(0.03125 - 0.02) / 0.02 = 56.25\\%$.",
            "generic": "Not quite. Divide the excess by the intended update.",
            "byKey": {
              "ratio": "That is the ratio of the two updates; subtract 1."
            }
          },
          "explain": {
            "text": "$0.01125 / 0.02 = 56.25\\%$ too large."
          }
        },
        {
          "question": "Starting from the stored weight of part 2, a hundred updates of $+0.01$ are applied in bf16. What is the weight at the end? Give the decimal.",
          "widget": {
            "kind": "numeric",
            "answer": 6.03125,
            "tol": {
              "abs": 1e-09
            },
            "wrong": [
              {
                "id": "exact",
                "value": 7.03125,
                "tol": {
                  "abs": 1e-09
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "start",
                "value": 6,
                "tol": {
                  "abs": 1e-09
                }
              }
            ],
            "label": "Weight"
          },
          "feedback": {
            "correct": "Each $+0.01$ is under half the gap, 0.015625, and rounds away: still 6.03125.",
            "generic": "Not quite. Compare 0.01 with half the gap.",
            "byKey": {
              "exact": "That is the exact result, which a float32 master copy would reach.",
              "start": "The weight is 6.03125 after part 2."
            }
          },
          "explain": {
            "text": "Rounding made one update 56.25% too large and erased the next hundred: the weight stays at 6.03125."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
